        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Draft label written by Kate Hay/Sarah Medlam 1996.\nArmchair.\nBritain; about 1760\nMahogany; modern upholstery\nSimilar chairs, described as 'French Chairs' are illustrated in Thomas Chippendale's<i> The Gentleman &amp; Cabinet-Maker's Director</i>, (3rd edition 1762), plate XIX. The chairs illustrated have upholstered backs and seats and could have either straight or cabriole (curved) legs. []"@en ;
